It was my quarter.

268
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,330
Was it her quarter?

269
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:31,750
How about we talk about this over dinner?

270
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:35,720
- Okay, lady, you're out of here.     - No, you can't arrest me!

271
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,010
I won't go back to that hellhole!

272
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:42,260
I'm just taking you outside.

273
00:17:42,470 --> 00:17:43,970
Oh, okay.

274
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:52,940
I need something old, something new, something borrowed and something blue.

275
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:56,360
Here's something blue and new.

276
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:59,030
You are so efficient. I love you.

277
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:00,700
- Let's go.     - No, wait!

278
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:02,450
We need something old.

279
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:06,500
I have a condom in my wallet that I've had since I was 12.

280
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,040
That'll work.

281
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:11,920
I don't think so.

282
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,590
Now something borrowed.

283
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:20,090
- Here, just take this.     - That's stealing.

284
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:22,850
We'll bring it back. Put it under your dress.

285
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,400
Aw.

286
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,480
Okay. One thing at a time.

287
00:18:48,910 --> 00:18:52,380
- Are you gonna play?     - No, I don't really have any money.

288
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:56,170
Not yet, anyway.

289
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,380
Can't sit here if you don't play.

290
00:19:13,770 --> 00:19:17,530
Hello. My name is Regina Phalange.

291
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,030
I'm a businesswoman in town on business.

292
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:24,030
Would you like to see my card?

293
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:25,990
What did I do with my Filofax?

294
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,450
I must've left it in Conference Room B.

295
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:31,580
- Fourteen.     - Hit me.

296
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:37,630
Oh, my God. May I just say that you gentlemen have the exact same hands?

297
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:40,510
They're identical.

298
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:43,430
I've never seen that in the business world.

299
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,800
Stop it.

300
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:52,560
Miss Phalange, may I ask you a question as an impartial person at this table?

301
00:19:52,770 --> 00:19:54,310
Please stop it.

302
00:19:56,150 --> 00:19:59,150
Wouldn't you pay good money to see identical hands...

303
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:03,780
...showcased in some type of an entertainment venue?

304
00:20:03,990 --> 00:20:07,870
If you leave now, I will chop off my hand and give it to you!

305
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:12,620
Didn't I just throw you out?

306
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,960
No, you threw out Phoebe.

307
00:20:15,210 --> 00:20:18,000
I'm Regina Phalange. Phalange.

308
00:20:18,590 --> 00:20:20,380
Come on, lady.

309
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:21,920
Please take him too.

310
00:20:22,130 --> 00:20:24,800
Me? Oh, come on, man.

311
00:20:25,010 --> 00:20:26,260
Come on, buddy.

312
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,390
Don't let him do this. Come on!

313
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:32,270
I'm your hand twin!

314
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:38,730
Hello. One marriage, please.

315
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:40,400
We want to get married.

316
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:43,280
There's a service in progress. Have a seat.

317
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,110
All right.

318
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,250
What are you doing?

319
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:58,000
The "Wedding March." Does that freak you out?

320
00:20:58,210 --> 00:21:00,090
No, it's the graduation song.

321
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:06,220
Okay.

322
00:21:06,430 --> 00:21:09,260
This is it. We're gonna get married.

323
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,060
You sure you wanna do this?

324
00:21:16,730 --> 00:21:18,980
Hello, Mrs. Ross!

325
00:21:19,230 --> 00:21:22,320
Well, hello, Mr. Rachel!

326
00:21:24,490 --> 00:21:26,280
Wait. Okay.

